                "quote_count": 0,
                "quoted_status_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_id": null,
                "quoted_status_profile_username": null,
                "reply_count": 1,
                "retweet_count": 2,
                "source": "Twitter for iPhone",
                "text": "If Republicans can afford to extend tax cuts for the wealthiest Americans, they should be able to extend tax credits that make health insurance affordable for more than 20 million Americans.\n\nDemocracy is supposed to be noisy, but at the end of the day, reasonable people should be able to come to reasonable agreements through good-faith negotiation. That\u2019s all we were asking for: a negotiation. However, you can't negotiate with a party that is subservient to the President.\n\nRepublicans had months to negotiate with us leading up to the shutdown. Had they done so instead of taking their marching orders from the President, we may not have found ourselves in the circumstances of the last six weeks.\n\nMy full statement on last night's government funding vote: https://t.co/mUn8SCmJMX",
                "text_lang": "en",
                "text_tagged_users": null,
                "text_tagged_users_ids": null,
                "text_tags": null,
                "timestamp": 1763053012,
                "view_count": 541
